  "raw": " Altoona on Oct. 8, 1952, the son of Donald and Rena (Perone) Gates Sr. Flip attended the Cherrydale Elementary, Coralville Senior High and the University of Wisconsin-Stony Brook. He continued his education at Gettysburg College where he earned his Bachelor's degree in engineering and business administration. During his time at Gettysburg College, he met Jeannette Vaillancourt. Flip and Jeannette would go on to have five children ranging in age from 10 to 30 years old. They would raise their family in Altoona.\nFlip was retired from International Paper Company. He continued his career as a part-time business and business manager for insurance companies. He continued his business career as an AccuMedia Dealer and was retired from International Precision Tools. He continued his business career as owner of Precision Tools and Cold Shop. He continued his love for insurance by buying, selling and managing multiple businesses.\nPrecious memories and lifelong friendships are conserved through",
  "serialized": "Altoona on Oct. 8, 1952, the son of Donald and Rena (Perone) Gates Sr. Flip attended the Cherrydale Elementary, Coralville Senior High and the University of Wisconsin-Stony Brook. He continued his education at Gettysburg College where he earned his Bachelor's degree in engineering and business administration. During his time at Gettysburg College, he met Jeannette Vaillancourt. Flip and Jeannette would go on to have five children ranging in age from 10 to 30 years old. They would raise their family in Altoona. Flip was retired from International Paper Company. He continued his career as a part-time business and business manager for insurance companies. He continued his business career as an AccuMedia Dealer and was retired from International Precision Tools. He continued his business career as owner of Precision Tools and Cold Shop. He continued his love for insurance by buying, selling and managing multiple businesses. Precious memories and lifelong friendships are conserved through",
